  "finding": "TWO settled facts. (1) CHECKBOX DIRTY FOCUS-OUT: a toggled (dirty) CheckBox losing focus fires BeforeUpdate -> AfterUpdate -> Exit, exactly like a TextBox. Rows (checkbox_dirty_focus_out): TextBox1 Exit (clean, no BeforeUpdate) -> CheckBox1 Enter(False) -> Change(Value True) -> Click(Value True) -> BeforeUpdate(Cancel False) -> AfterUpdate -> Exit(Cancel False) -> TextBox2 Enter. So the focus-out validation MUST treat a dirty CheckBox like a dirty TextBox (queue BeforeUpdate/AfterUpdate before Exit). Also: a CheckBox DOES expose Enter/Exit/BeforeUpdate/AfterUpdate (FM20_EVENT_FACTS.md previously treated these as unknown for MdcCheckBoxEvents). (2) NET-VALUE / OldValue is a NON-GOAL: an edit-then-revert (type a char, Backspace back to the value-at-focus-gain, net change = none) STILL fires BeforeUpdate + AfterUpdate on focus-out. Rows (edit_revert_focus_out): KeyDown(231=VK_PACKET) -> Change(X) -> KeyUp -> KeyDown(8=Backspace) -> Change(empty) -> KeyUp -> BeforeUpdate(False) -> AfterUpdate -> Exit -> TextBox2 Enter. So MSForms uses the sticky edited-since flag, NOT a net-value-vs-baseline gate -- the OxForms sticky dirty flag (esq.7) is already faithful, and the OldValue/net-value refinement is dropped.",
  "driving_method": "Computer-use vision (precise clicks + keystrokes) on a background-COM-hosted Excel running the committed w008-checkbox-update fixture; each scenario was a separate ClearLog -> Show -> SetW008Scenario* -> drive -> export-worksheet run, so the per-run sequence restarts at 1. The edit-revert keystroke was injected via VK_PACKET (KeyCode 231), a computer-use type() artifact -- the load-bearing facts are the Change/BeforeUpdate/AfterUpdate firings, not the KeyCode value. This fixture mutates no argument; it only observes whether the events fire.",
